      "evidence": {
        "source": "manual_review",
        "cve_id": null,
        "description": "Resembles IDOR: a helper that looks up an EmployeeProfile by a caller-supplied employee_id, which a scanner may flag as object access keyed on user input. It is actually safe: the lookup is performed against visible_employees_for(user), a tenant/role-scoped queryset (HR/payroll see all; managers see only direct reports plus self; employees see only themselves; unauthenticated gets an empty queryset). An attacker guessing another employee's id falls through to get_object_or_404 with no matching row, so ownership scoping is enforced at the query level."
